  partName: Spark Plug (6)
  description: The Spark Plug (6) is a tiny, elongated component positioned at the
    top-right-rear of the engine, made of Material.001, which produces the high-voltage
    spark necessary for combustion. Its elongated shape allows it to reach deep into
    the combustion chamber, ensuring efficient ignition, and an interesting detail
    is that it is designed to be replaced periodically to maintain optimal engine
    performance. The spark plug's material properties enable it to operate effectively
    in the high-temperature environment of the engine.
  audioExplanation: {fileID: 0}
